{comment: Verse 1 — a letter that says: let us play}
[D]A DIP is just a [A]letter that says, let us play —
[Bm]no budget line for miracles, [G]no rider for the soul.
[D]You read it in Bogotá [A]and you answered with a yes,
[Bm]and a chiva full of strangers [G]found the first place to be whole.

{comment: Chorus}
[G]Thank you, Devcon — [D]for every single yes.
[A]Bogotá to Bangkok to [D]Buenos Aires to Bombay,
[G]you kept giving us a room [D]and we kept filling it with people —
[A]the orchestra is whoever shows up, and [D]you let them show up every day.

{comment: Verse 2 — Bangkok}
[D]Bangkok, twenty twenty-four, a [A]Music Stage inside the hall,
[Bm]a chair where the road of [G]the orchestra crossed someone else's road.
[D]You could have booked a headline [A]act — you booked an open circle,
[Bm]and the open circle paid you [G]back in every song it owed.

{comment: Verse 3 — Buenos Aires}
[D]Buenos Aires, the river wide, [A]the tradition one year older,
[Bm]another yes, another floor, [G]another ring of borrowed drums.
[D]Every city you said yes [A]in, the circle learned a language,
[Bm]and carried it like luggage [G]to wherever the next one comes.

{comment: Chorus}
(repeat)

{comment: Verse 4 — Bombay, DIP eight-five-seven-six}
[D]Then Bombay — eight five seven [A]six on the Culture Track —
[Bm]cane stools and rugs and a [G]mandala of light on the wall.
[D]Four days, thirty-five artists, and on [A]the last night your own lamp,
[Bm]your own confetti, your own closing, in [G]the room you let us build at all.

{comment: Verse 5 — the people who built the room}
[D]We saw you arm in arm [A]when the final song was over,
[Bm]the ones who carried cases, [G]pulled the cables, found the keys.
[D]We made you a little [A]book of your own photographers' pictures,
[Bm]because thank you is a small word [G]for four days of yeses like these.

{comment: Bridge — Lisbon}
[D]Now the road turns [A]toward Lisbon, October twenty twenty-seven,
[Bm]and this time the [G]letter won't arrive alone.
[D]A whole community is writing it — [A]the hosts, the hands, the ʻohana —
[Bm]so the next room has [G]more people holding up the dome.
[D]We're not asking for a [A]stage. We're asking for a floor.
[Bm]We'll post it soon, and if you [G]say yes, we'll fill it like before.

{comment: Last chorus}
[G]Thank you, Devcon — [D]for every single yes.
[A]Bogotá to Bangkok to [D]Buenos Aires to Bombay,
[G]and whatever Lisbon answers, we [D]will play with open doors —
[A]the orchestra is whoever shows up, [D]and you showed up too. Olé. 🎻
